            <ArticleTitle>Coronary ostial stenosis after aortic valve replacement, revisited.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2169-71</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary artery occlusive disease that develops after an uncomplicated aortic valve replacement is well recognized. We present a case that required two further coronary operations and two salvage angioplasty procedures for a continuing fibrotic process in the ascending aorta. The literature and pathology are reviewed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
